# Context files are strategist-authored — do not edit

The following files in this repository are behavioral context for AI agents.
They are authored and maintained by Hassan and Computer (the strategist AI).
**Implementing agents (Cursor, Claude Code) must never modify them**, even
when fixing seemingly-related issues, even when they appear out of date.

## Files you must not edit

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `AGENTS.md` | Repo-level instructions for any AI agent |
| `CLAUDE.md` | Claude Code specific instructions |
| `.cursorrules` | Legacy Cursor pointer file |
| `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` | Modern Cursor structured rules |
| `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` | PR description template |
| `.editorconfig` | Cross-editor formatting |
| `.gitignore` | Git ignore rules |
| `.env.example` | Documentation of required env vars |

## What to do if you think a context file is wrong

1. **Stop.** Do not edit the file.
2. **Add a `// TODO(hassan):` comment in your PR description**, explaining:
   - Which file you think needs to change
   - What you think it should say
   - Why (with reference to the active prompt)
3. **Continue implementing the prompt as written.** If the missing context
   meant you couldn't complete the prompt, mark the relevant Definition of
   Done items as blocked and explain.

## Why this rule exists

These files act as **persistent system-prompt injection** across many Cursor
sessions. The whole reason this project uses Cursor + Claude Code instead of
Replit Agent is that they reliably respect stable context files. If
implementing agents are allowed to edit them, that stability evaporates —
constraints drift session over session and prompts stop being reliable.

The only sanctioned way these files change is: Hassan and the strategist
explicitly update them between prompt runs, outside of any implementation
work.
